  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When aqueous solution of borax <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is acidified<br />with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>, we get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> as follows</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mrow><mi>Borox</mi></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HCl</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>Boric</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>acid</mi></mrow></munder></math></p><p>Boric acid is not a proticacid it does not give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> ion accepts a pair of electrons and acts as a Lewis acid.</p>"
  }
